# AI Extraction Guidelines

This file is optional. If present as `template.md` (copy this file and rename it), its
content is appended to the AI's system prompt for every message classified by
`--ai-filter`. Use it to steer classification/extraction without touching code.

`template.md` is gitignored — put personal context here freely (names, interests,
group-specific jargon) without worrying about it being committed.

The base categories, required fields, and output schema are always enforced regardless
of what you write here; this file can only add guidance, not override the schema.

## Example sections you might include

### Priorities
List topics/activities you care most about, so ambiguous messages lean toward higher
importance when they touch these:
- e.g. "Badminton and climbing sessions are high priority."

### Glossary
Define group-specific abbreviations or jargon so the AI doesn't misread them:
- e.g. "B+ = Boulder+ (a climbing gym chain). USC = University Sports Centre."

### People to weight
Note organizers/admins whose messages are usually more authoritative than casual chat:
- e.g. "Messages from the house committee (exco) are usually official announcements."

### Extra ignore rules
Beyond the default ignore rule (casual/irrelevant chatter), name any other patterns
you want auto-ignored:
- e.g. "Ignore messages that are just a single emoji or 'ok'/'noted'/'thanks'."

### Locale
State a default timezone/locale if relevant times are otherwise ambiguous:
- e.g. "Assume Singapore time (UTC+8) unless a message states otherwise."

### Style preferences
Any formatting preference for the summary field:
- e.g. "Keep summaries under 20 words. Always include a payment amount if mentioned."

## Special sections (parsed structurally, not just free text)

Unlike the sections above (which are just appended to the AI's prompt as guidance), the
two sections below are actually parsed by the app. Their headings must match exactly.

### `## Folders to query`

When neither `--chat` nor `--folder` is given on the command line, every folder listed
here is processed in one run instead of requiring a separate invocation per folder.
Folder names must match your real Telegram folder names exactly (unlike the substring
matching used for ignored chats/topics below):

```markdown
## Folders to query
- Helix House
- NUS Modules
```

### `## Ignored chats`

Any chat whose name contains one of these entries (case-insensitive substring match) is
skipped entirely before any AI call is made - zero cost, not just hidden output. This
also matches a Telegram forum topic's name for chats that use the forum/topics feature,
so you can ignore just one topic within a chat while the rest of that chat is still
processed normally:

```markdown
## Ignored chats
- Laundry
- Marketplace
```

